 61GA c  {+61}Ga isotope produced in the fragmentation of 70 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr
 61GA2c  beam with Ni target. Fragments selected with the LISE3 separator at    
 61GA3c  GANIL and identified by time-of-flight and energy loss. Measured       
 61GA4c  half-life of {+61}Ga ground-state decay by (fragment)|b, (fragment)|g  
 61GA5c  correlations using set of four Si detectors (an energy loss |DE        
 61GA6c  detector, a degrade, DSSD and Si(Li)) for particles surrounded by      
 61GA7c  four HPGe Clover detectors, three EXOGAM and one mini-clover Ge        
 61GA8c  detector for |g rays.                                                  
